# Optional environment for wmr-bridge.service.
# Copy to /etc/wmr-bridge/wmr-bridge.env (or let pi/install.sh create it).
#
# Pass extra CLI flags without editing the systemd unit (for example, single-hand
# mode on a dedicated Pi):
# WMR_BRIDGE_ARGS=--hand left
#
# The unit passes --token-file /etc/wmr-bridge/token. That file must be owned by
# the service user (chown wmr:wmr, mode 640), otherwise the daemon cannot read
# it and systemd restarts it. The wmr group can read it, so add an admin who
# runs pi/tools/wifi_probe.py to that group. To use an environment variable
# instead, remove --token-file from ExecStart and set:
# WMR_BRIDGE_TOKEN=change-me
#
# Never commit a real token.
